      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface expression confirmed by confocal microscopy (YFP total pool + BTX647 surface pool) and flow cytometry (surface signal up to 100-fold above threshold in YFP-positive cells). Multiple additional ledger lines (PMC3861077, PMC6465299) state the HA-hERG S1\u2013S2 construct 'does not interfere with processing and function', corroborating that this loop tolerates insertions without functional disruption.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "Python verification confirms seq[435]='T' and seq[436]='E', matching the paper's stated T436/E437 junction exactly. Position 436 lies within the extracellular S1\u2013S2 span (landmarks 430\u2013453), 7 residues from the TM1 C-terminus (429) and 17 residues from the TM2 N-terminus (454), well clear of both TM boundaries. Two independent papers pin this exact junction, and surface display of the full-length membrane-anchored channel was validated by both confocal microscopy and flow cytometry. Two independent studies (PMC5917007 and PMC10568093) both report insertion of a 13-residue bungarotoxin-binding site (BBS) between T436 and E437 in the extracellular S1\u2013S2 loop of full-length, membrane-anchored hERG (KCNH2). The construct BBS-hERG-YFP was expressed in HEK293 cells and surface-labeled with Alexa Fluor 647-conjugated bungarotoxin in non-permeabilized cells. [validation: surface_and_function; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 29725305,
          "citation": "PMID 29725305",
          "claim": "A 13-residue bungarotoxin-binding site (BBS; TGGCGGTACTACGAGAGCAGCCTGGAGCCCTACCCCGAC) ( Sekine-Aizawa and Huganir, 2004 ; Yang et al., 2010 ) was then introduced between residues T436/E437 in the extracellular S1\u2013S2 loop of hERG using the Quik-Change Lightning Site-Directed Mutagenesis Kit (Stratagene) according to the manufacturer's instructions. 16 LQT2 mutations were introduced in the PAS domain of BBS-hERG-YFP via site-directed mutagenesis."
        }
      ],
