      "rationale": "Python verification confirms seq[442]='T' and seq[443]='E', matching the paper's stated T443/E444 junction exactly. Position 443 lies within the extracellular S1\u2013S2 span (landmarks 430\u2013453), 14 residues from the TM1 C-terminus (429) and 10 residues from the TM2 N-terminus (454). Although C445 is two residues downstream of E444, the paper explicitly reports this insertion in the full-length channel and uses it for surface labeling, demonstrating the tag is tolerated at this junction despite proximity to the disulfide-forming cysteines. DOI:10.1101/2020.02.17.952606 reports insertion of a 17-residue HA-containing sequence (NSEHYPYDVPDYAVTFE; 9 aa HA tag with 4 aa linkers on each side) between T443 and E444 in the extracellular S1\u2013S2 region of full-length KCNH2 (KV11.1) by inverse PCR. The construct was used for surface-labeling studies of the intact membrane-anchored channel. [validation: surface_only; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
