  "literature_notes": "All ledger evidence for KCNH2 converges on the extracellular S1\u2013S2 loop (topology landmarks 430\u2013453). Two junctions are explicitly pinned by residue number: T436/E437 (BBS, PMC5917007 + PMC10568093) and T443/E444 (HA, DOI:10.1101/2020.02.17.952606). Five additional ledger lines (PMC7704534, PMC3861077, PMC3877390, PMC6465299, PMC13182972) confirm HA-tag tolerance in the S1\u2013S2 loop without naming a specific residue; these are subsumed by the two pinned sites above and do not constitute independent region-level sites because the loop is already represented by two validated junctions. No ledger evidence supports any insertion in the other extracellular spans (501\u2013501, single residue; 571\u2013638, S3\u2013S4 turret/pore loop) or at either terminus (N-terminus is intracellular residues 1\u2013408; C-terminus is intracellular residues 657\u20131159). The single-residue extracellular span at 501 is too short for any insertion. The S3\u2013S4/turret region (571\u2013638) contains the selectivity filter and pore helix and is not supported by any ledger insertion.",
